    "overview": {
      "body": "The deep erg is not empty in the comforting sense. It is empty in the Arrakis sense: exposed, watchful, and full of consequences for anyone who assumes distance means safety."
    },
    "settlement": {
      "body": "The biome resists ordinary colony thinking. Rock is scarce, plant life is thin, and the map pushes the player toward temporary work, disciplined crossings, and careful staging rather than casual expansion."
    },
    "wormCountry": {
      "body": "Most importantly, the deep erg teaches the player where makers truly belong. Open sand is not a neutral floor. It is active territory that answers labor, movement, and noise."
    }
  },
